     "explanation": "Multiply the numerator and denominator by the conjugate $4+\\sqrt{7}$. The denominator becomes $(4-\\sqrt{7})(4+\\sqrt{7})=16-7=9$, giving $\\frac{4+\\sqrt{7}}{9}$."
